From 46db525892073ed247c5bf2db203e0d511a5439d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: powerfulghost <powerfulghost42@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 03:18:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] gfx906 correctness: fix silent corruption in the q8-multi
 grouped plan (non-adjacent members)

T8 grouped up to 3 repacked-Q8_0 c=1 mat-vecs sharing src1 with NO adjacency
requirement. The grouped kernel writes every member's output at the head's
node position, extending each member output's live range back to the head.
ggml's memory planner computes liveness for the *unfused* schedule, so a
non-adjacent member's output buffer may already be reused for a tensor that is
live between head and member -> the early write corrupts unrelated state.

Measured symptom: builds/tp-multi answered "The capital of France is" with
' payFEFEFEFEFEFE...' on any prompt (Oct-14 builds/tp without T8 was fine);
llama-perplexity -b 1 read 1943116 instead of ~4.21. Everything E2..E7 on
that build inherited the corruption and their "byte-identical" checks were
comparing corrupted output to corrupted output.

Fix: q8m_build_plan only groups graph-adjacent members (idx == head_idx + n),
so no node can sit between head and member. After the fix: coherent output,
PPL -b1 = 4.2120 (identical to GFX906_Q8_MULTI_OFF=1), 256-token greedy
byte-identical ON/OFF; tg128 gain drops to ~+0.5% (noise-edge).

Also guards f32m_build_plan (T10, default off) with the same adjacency rule
(same hazard class), and corrects the hc-up-pre.cuh comment: the hc chain is
